Subject: [HW-08 candidate] Iris: release OPP votes for a zero rate request

Do not turn a power-off request into the minimum enabled operating point.
Use the existing NULL-OPP release API, retaining ceil lookup for nonzero
rates and propagating both release and lookup errors.

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_resources.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_resources.c
index 2c4d34c7bd77d1f78d3572f659da656eb3b12113..91216a44c7b95a50710ead7f8b51ff34855ee93c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_resources.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_resources.c
@@ -61,9 +61,13 @@ int iris_unset_icc_bw(struct iris_core *core)
 
 int iris_opp_set_rate(struct device *dev, unsigned long freq)
 {
-	struct dev_pm_opp *opp __free(put_opp) =
-		devfreq_recommended_opp(dev, &freq, 0);
+	struct dev_pm_opp *opp __free(put_opp) = NULL;
 
+	/* A zero request releases votes; a ceil lookup would select min OPP. */
+	if (!freq)
+		return dev_pm_opp_set_opp(dev, NULL);
+
+	opp = devfreq_recommended_opp(dev, &freq, 0);
 	if (IS_ERR(opp))
 		return PTR_ERR(opp);
 
